<!-- VERIFIEDPRESS.ORG -->
<div id="verifiedpress-dialog" class="w3-modal">
    <div class="w3-modal-content">
        <div class="w3-container w3-white">
            <h2 class="w3-blue">🔐 VerifiedPress.org Terms of Service</h2>
              <p>
                <ul class="w3-ul">
                    <li><b>Effective Date:</b> July 17, 2025</li>
                    <li><b>Last Updated:</b> July 17, 2025</li>
                </ul>
                <h4>🧭 1. Overview</h4>
                <p>VerifiedPress.org (“VerifiedPress”, “we”, “our”, “us”) provides infrastructure for decentralized identity, credential registries, and role-based verification for contributors in the press ecosystem—including journalists, editors, independent authors, and AI entities.</p>
                <p>By accessing or using our services, users (“you”, “your”) agree to be bound by these Terms. These Terms form a legal agreement governing registry participation, credential interactions, and role attestation.</p>
                <h4>🧑‍💻 2. Eligibility and Contributor Roles</h4>
                <p>You may interact with VerifiedPress if you:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Are a human, organization, or AI agent submitting identity metadata for press-related activity</li>
                  <li>Hold valid decentralized identifiers (DIDs) or credentials aligned with registry schemas</li>
                  <li>Agree to comply with provenance, role-based, and verification standards</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We reserve the right to restrict roles based on verification, credential revocation, or governance decisions.</p>
                <h4>🛠️ 3. Use of Services</h4>
                <p>Permitted uses include:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Publishing or resolving DID documents</li>
                  <li>Linking press credentials and role metadata</li>
                  <li>Discovering public contributor profiles</li>
                  <li>Verifying provenance and credential integrity</li>
                </ul>
                <p>You must not:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Submit false or deceptive metadata</li>
                  <li>Bypass registry rules or role validations</li>
                  <li>Use the service for surveillance, profiling, or harassment</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We support opt-in resolution and decentralized privacy preferences.</p>
                <h4>🛡️ 4. Intellectual Property</h4>
                <p>You retain ownership of identity data and metadata submitted to VerifiedPress. By participating, you grant us a limited license to:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Index publicly resolvable metadata</li>
                  <li>Anchor role and credential summaries for discoverability</li>
                  <li>Host registry snapshots via decentralized networks</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Credential schemas, method specifications, and governance docs are licensed under permissive open-source terms.</p>
                <h4>🔍 5. Privacy and Data Handling</h4>
                <p>We process only minimal identity metadata required for resolution and verification. No behavioral profiling, tracking, or advertising occurs. For full details, see our [Privacy Policy](https://privacy-policy.page).</p>
                <h4>🧾 6. Registry and Credential Integrity</h4>
                <p>VerifiedPress may:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Deny indexing of unverifiable metadata</li>
                  <li>Flag revoked credentials</li>
                  <li>Apply governance-defined status labels</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Contributor rights include:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Metadata updates</li>
                  <li>Revocation requests</li>
                  <li>Credential reissuance</li>
                </ul>
                <p>All changes are cryptographically auditable.</p>
                <h4>👥 7. Governance and Dispute Resolution</h4>
                <p>VerifiedPress operates under open governance. Any disputes should be directed to:<br/>
                  <a href="mailto:presspage.entertainment@gmail.com?subject=Governance%20and%20Dispute%20Resolution">📮 `presspage.entertainment@gmail.com`</a>
                </p>
                <p>Resolutions will follow transparent protocols and decentralized recordkeeping.</p>
                <h4>📌 8. Changes to These Terms</h4>
                <p>We may update these Terms for legal, technical, or governance reasons. Material changes will be announced via the registry and contributor communication channels.</p>
                <p>Continued use after updates constitutes acceptance.</p>
                <h4>🌐 Contact Us</h4>
                <p>For questions, feedback, or governance matters:<br/> 
                  <a href="mailto:presspage.entertainment@gmail.com?subject=Re:%20VERIFIEDPRESS.ORG%20Terms%20of%20Service">📮 `presspage.entertainment@gmail.com`</a>
                </p>
            </p>
            <button class="w3-button w3-block w3-black" onclick="document.getElementById('verifiedpress-dialog').style.display='none';">OK</button>
            <br/>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


